  <issue>
  Convert Recordings list to infinite scrollers
## Is your feature request related to a problem?

Currently we have pagination on our recordings lists allowing you to paginate through results in batches of 20. This has some flaws however:
1. We cannot guarantee that the next page is the correct offset as we offset by number, not time. This affects any relative date ranges as new recordings entering the list change the offset.
2. We are limited on our ability to do things like autoplay constantly as the list comes to an end. Does the next autoplay, paginate the list?
3. Showing new recordings coming in has the same problem, we have to change back to the first page of results which breaks the flow.

## Describe the solution you'd like

Ditch pagination all-together and replace it with an infinite scroller.

**Pros**
* Greatly simplifies the logic. Pagination is just "fetch recordings older than the oldest in the list or newer than the newest".
* Fixes the off-by-1 errors that occur as new recordings appear in the overall queryset
* Makes "autoplay" simple in both directions as we just load more when we hit the end of the list

**Cons**
* No fixed url for pagination - refreshes by default would just go back to the top
* No quick way to jump through multiple pages (currently you can just click multiple times to paginate back - although this is currently buggy as well)

## Describe alternatives you've considered



## Additional context

User feedback on this (paraphrased):
"I like pagination, it allows me to quickly jump back multiple pages. Without this I would have to change the date range filter which is way too many clicks. Switch to have both options would be best. If I know there was a time that people did a particular action, I can just paginate back."



#### *Thank you* for your feature request – we love each and every one!
